{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":7859,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"SEEDED","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"This is a family of proteins conserved from fungi to humans, including fungal Inclusion body clearance protein Iml2 protein, animal tetratricopeptide repeat protein 39A/B/C (TT39A/B/C) and some uncharacterised proteins. Members of this family carry a tetratricopeptide repeat [pfam:PF07719] at their C terminus. This entry includes Iml2 and its paralogue-YKR018C from S. cerevisiae; Iml2 localises to the cytoplasm and nucleus [[cite:PUB00016470]], and its expression is increased in response to DNA replication stress [[cite:PUB00066967]]. It is found to be involved in lipid droplet-mediated inclusion body clearing after protein folding stress [[cite:PUB00088292]]. In humans, TTC39A (also known as DEME6) is expressed in primary breast carcinomas but not in normal breast tissue, and has a putative eukaryotic RNP-1 RNA binding region and a candidate anchoring transmembrane domain. It is coordinately regulated with oestrogen receptor, but is not necessarily oestradiol-responsive [[cite:PUB00044224]]. TTC39B has been linked to lipid metabolism [[cite:PUB00072592]].","domain_architectures":143,"interpro_id":"IPR019412","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":9867,"name":"Iml2/Tetratricopeptide repeat protein 39","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF10300","proteins":9006,"proteomes":2835,"short_name":"Iml2-TPR_39","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF10300","structures":0,"taxa":7559,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[